  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37130542",
      "title": "Introducing Variables",
      "lectureOrder": 40,
      "videoOrder": 37,
      "sourceHash": "88641396724fc41d721692bf3335a7feb1b4068f90170cefeca3450705e15217",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 4.2,
          "en": "So we learned about custom widgets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.2,
          "end": 6.06,
          "en": "A super important feature you're going",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.06,
          "end": 9.33,
          "en": "to use all the time when working with flutter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.33,
          "end": 12.303,
          "en": "Now there's one thing you can do with custom widgets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.303,
          "end": 14.94,
          "en": "that makes them even more powerful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.94,
          "end": 17.52,
          "en": "But before we can explore that thing and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.52,
          "end": 20.34,
          "en": "before we then thereafter can come back to this app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.34,
          "end": 23.28,
          "en": "and add more features to that, we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.28,
          "end": 25.32,
          "en": "to dive into variables.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.32,
          "end": 27.96,
          "en": "So what are variables?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.96,
          "end": 30.21,
          "en": "Variables are data containers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.21,
          "end": 33.63,
          "en": "And this feature exists in basically all programming",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.63,
          "end": 35.7,
          "en": "languages because it turns out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.7,
          "end": 39.18,
          "en": "that in all programming languages you are working a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.18,
          "end": 41.73,
          "en": "with values, like also here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 41.73,
          "end": 44.85,
          "en": "where in our styled text we have some text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.85,
          "end": 48.42,
          "en": "or basically everywhere else, we have a bunch of widgets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.42,
          "end": 50.79,
          "en": "and configuration objects, which are",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.79,
          "end": 53.25,
          "en": "of course also all values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.25,
          "end": 55.56,
          "en": "Now to understand variables, let me go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 55.56,
          "end": 57.72,
          "en": "to the gradient container here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 57.72,
          "end": 60.69,
          "en": "and here we could say that maybe these alignments, which",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 60.69,
          "end": 63.33,
          "en": "of course also are values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 63.33,
          "end": 66.66,
          "en": "should not be stored here in this part of the code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 66.66,
          "end": 70.17,
          "en": "which is hidden quite a bit inside of the widget tree.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 70.17,
          "end": 72.78,
          "en": "But maybe we wanna define them up here at the beginning",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 72.78,
          "end": 74.91,
          "en": "of the file so that if we ever want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 74.91,
          "end": 76.32,
          "en": "to change these alignments,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 76.32,
          "end": 77.97,
          "en": "we can do it right here at the top",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 77.97,
          "end": 81.53999999999999,
          "en": "of the file without having to dive into our widgetry.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 81.53999999999999,
          "end": 84.455,
          "en": "This is of course just a convenience thing in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 84.455,
          "end": 87.75,
          "en": "but the more complex your code and project gets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 87.75,
          "end": 90.69,
          "en": "the more little tweaks like this could help.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 90.69,
          "end": 93.53999999999999,
          "en": "To do this we could cut the value from down there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 93.53999999999999,
          "end": 96.3,
          "en": "and instead store it in such a variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 96.3,
          "end": 100.41,
          "en": "because variables as you learned are data containers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 100.41,
          "end": 104.46000000000001,
          "en": "In dart they are created with help of the var keyword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 104.46000000000001,
          "end": 106.71000000000001,
          "en": "then the equal sign operator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 106.71000000000001,
          "end": 108.50999999999999,
          "en": "the so-called assignment operator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 108.50999999999999,
          "end": 110.52000000000001,
          "en": "and then the value that should be stored,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 110.52000000000001,
          "end": 112.56,
          "en": "for example, a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 112.56,
          "end": 116.4,
          "en": "So here, if I wanna store this alignment value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 116.4,
          "end": 119.75999999999999,
          "en": "I could create a variable here outside of my class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 119.75999999999999,
          "end": 121.56,
          "en": "We can also create it inside of the class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 121.56,
          "end": 123.862,
          "en": "but for the moment let's do it outside,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 123.862,
          "end": 126,
          "en": "then give it any name of your choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 126,
          "end": 128.807,
          "en": "Like for example, startAlignment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 129.69,
          "end": 131.79,
          "en": "The name is up to you, but just as",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 131.79,
          "end": 133.132,
          "en": "before with other names,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 133.132,
          "end": 136.35,
          "en": "it should not be separated into multiple words.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 136.35,
          "end": 138.42000000000002,
          "en": "Instead, words inside of words should start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 138.42000000000002,
          "end": 142.05,
          "en": "with an uppercase character, but unlike class names,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 142.05,
          "end": 144.32999999999998,
          "en": "the overall variable name should start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 144.32999999999998,
          "end": 145.8,
          "en": "with a lowercase character.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 145.8,
          "end": 147.982,
          "en": "So it should follow this naming pattern,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 147.982,
          "end": 150.69,
          "en": "and the name should describe which kind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 150.69,
          "end": 152.46,
          "en": "of value will be stored in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 152.46,
          "end": 154.96,
          "en": "that data container in that variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 154.96,
          "end": 157.86,
          "en": "And then we assign the value with an equal sign,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 157.86,
          "end": 160.953,
          "en": "in this case, alignment.topleft, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 161.83100000000002,
          "end": 164.4,
          "en": "So that's how we could define a variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 164.4,
          "end": 166.77,
          "en": "We could then add a second variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 166.77,
          "end": 169.89,
          "en": "and that is this end variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 169.89,
          "end": 172.3,
          "en": "So therefore I'll name this one endAlignment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 173.915,
          "end": 177.78,
          "en": "and store Alignment.bottomRight and there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 177.78,
          "end": 179.94,
          "en": "And with those two variables added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 179.94,
          "end": 183.24,
          "en": "we could use them down there to assign startAlignment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 183.24,
          "end": 188.24,
          "en": "as a value to begin and here endAlignment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 188.61,
          "end": 190.263,
          "en": "as a value to end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 191.13,
          "end": 192.42,
          "en": "Though here you will notice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 192.42,
          "end": 194.79,
          "en": "that I'm now getting an error that a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 194.79,
          "end": 197.88,
          "en": "of type null can't be assigned to a parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 197.88,
          "end": 200.46,
          "en": "of type AlignmentGeometry.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 200.46,
          "end": 202.41,
          "en": "This is a bit cryptic to understand though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 202.41,
          "end": 203.76,
          "en": "What does it mean?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 203.76,
          "end": 207.3,
          "en": "Well, variables when created with the var keyword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 207.3,
          "end": 210.9,
          "en": "which we're doing, here can actually be reassigned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 210.9,
          "end": 213.6,
          "en": "Here I'm assigning an initial value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 213.6,
          "end": 215.43,
          "en": "but I could then change that value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 215.43,
          "end": 217.89,
          "en": "For example, here in the build method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 217.89,
          "end": 222.89,
          "en": "Here, I could set startAlignment to Alignment.center.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 223.636,
          "end": 227.82,
          "en": "That's a core mechanism of variables created with var,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 227.82,
          "end": 229.713,
          "en": "you can reassign them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 230.7,
          "end": 234.48,
          "en": "Now, that's in the end where this error is coming from.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 234.48,
          "end": 237.09,
          "en": "This null part can be confusing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 237.09,
          "end": 240.66,
          "en": "but it actually also tells us that the const keyword seems",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 240.66,
          "end": 242.97,
          "en": "to be the problem that we might wanna remove",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 242.97,
          "end": 244.47,
          "en": "this const keyword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 244.47,
          "end": 247.41,
          "en": "and here it's referring to this const keyword in front",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 247.41,
          "end": 248.64,
          "en": "of BoxDecoration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 248.64,
          "end": 252.03,
          "en": "Since if we add cons here, it's also implicitly added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 252.03,
          "end": 253.44,
          "en": "to LinearGradient,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 253.44,
          "end": 256.653,
          "en": "and that is the object that takes begin and end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 257.61,
          "end": 261.66,
          "en": "Since the values of these variables could be changed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 261.66,
          "end": 265.68,
          "en": "it's not guaranteed to be stable, it's not guaranteed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 265.68,
          "end": 267.12,
          "en": "to be constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 267.12,
          "end": 269.97,
          "en": "and that's exactly the kind of problem we're facing here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 269.97,
          "end": 272.82,
          "en": "if we do have const in front of LinearGradient",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 272.82,
          "end": 277.38,
          "en": "or BoxDecoration, we can't tell Dart that it can cache",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 277.38,
          "end": 279.24,
          "en": "and reuse that value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 279.24,
          "end": 282.93,
          "en": "because actually these variables are not locked in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 282.93,
          "end": 285.06,
          "en": "They could change potentially, and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 285.06,
          "end": 287.76,
          "en": "therefore reusing this value would be unsafe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 287.76,
          "end": 291.72,
          "en": "because Dart might accidentally reuse an outdated value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 291.72,
          "end": 294.9,
          "en": "which is why you can't use const here then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 294.9,
          "end": 296.19,
          "en": "You could add it in front",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 296.19,
          "end": 300,
          "en": "of this list still since these colors are indeed locked in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 300,
          "end": 302.55,
          "en": "place here and hard coded here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 302.55,
          "end": 304.41,
          "en": "But that's the idea behind variables.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 304.41,
          "end": 307.664,
          "en": "We simply have data containers that store values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 307.664,
          "end": 309.288,
          "en": "and we can define them once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 309.288,
          "end": 312.51,
          "en": "and then use them multiple times wherever we want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 312.51,
          "end": 314.22,
          "en": "later in our code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 314.22,
          "end": 317.91,
          "en": "as long as that code has access to the variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 317.91,
          "end": 320.64300000000003,
          "en": "which here in this case is the case.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
